From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8953-xiaomi-markw: terminate charging at 150 mA

The battery node has no charge-term-current-microamp, so smbchg leaves
the PMI8950's termination current at its reset value, 300 mA. From a
500 mA USB port (SDP) the charge current is already below that in the
taper phase: on a Redmi 4 Prime the charger reported Full at 94 % after
a few minutes at 170-200 mA, recharged 100 mV lower and stopped again,
creeping up a percent at a time.

Set 150 mA, about C/27 for the 4000 mAh cell, so taper runs on to a
full battery from a USB port as well as from a wall charger.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
@@ -139,6 +139,7 @@
 &battery {
 	charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <4000000>;
+	charge-term-current-microamp = <150000>;
 	constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <1000000>;
 	voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
 	voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4380000>;
 };
